[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65866,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smooth muscle tumours of uncertain malignant potential (STUMPs) are tumours with features exceeding those of leiomyoma and its subtypes yet insufficient for a diagnosis of leiomyosarcoma that behave in a malignant fashion in only a minority of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65867,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8897/1 Smooth muscle tumour of uncertain malignant potential</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65868,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F9C &amp; XH1EN1 Neoplasms of unknown behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Smooth muscle tumour of uncertain malignant potential</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65869,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> atypical smooth muscle neoplasm</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65870,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65871,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lower genital tract, primarily vulvar and vaginal regions</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65872,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical features are nonspecific and include presentation as a patient-identified asymptomatic mass, symptoms related to a mass, and presentation as an incidental finding in the course of clinical evaluation of an unrelated condition {28786880}. Most tumours of uncertain malignant potential are malignant in only a minority of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65873,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Similar to uterine smooth muscle tumours, leiomyoma subtypes and leiomyosarcomas are less common than spindled leiomyomas in the lower genital tract.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65874,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65875,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>The pathogenesis is currently undefined for this location, but the pathogenetic mechanisms that underlie the development of STUMPs in the lower genital tract are presumably similar to those in other locations. See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/237\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Uterine leiomyoma</em>&nbsp;and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/241\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Smooth muscle tumour of uncertain malignant potential of the uterine corpus</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:04:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65876,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic appearance is heterogeneous, ranging from leiomyoma-like (whitish-tan and firm with a whorled cut surface) to leiomyosarcoma-like (whitish-tan and fleshy with variable necrosis and haemorrhage) {28786880; 28180147}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65877,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>STUMPs are tumours that are not unequivocally benign or malignant on the basis of histological criteria. Typically, the degree of cytological atypia, the mitotic count, and the presence of tumour cell necrosis are considered when evaluating and classifying smooth muscle tumours of the gynaecological tract {8179071}. As a result of some combination of these three features hindering classification as leiomyoma or leiomyosarcoma, &ldquo;smooth muscle tumour of uncertain malignant potential&rdquo; is often used as a diagnostic category to capture these tumours that have a low (yet non-zero) risk of recurrence {28786880; 28180147; 19417585}. Suggestions have been made to assess additional morphological features in cases of potential uterine STUMPs because of their association with adverse patient outcome. These features include atypical mitotic figures, epithelioid morphology, vascular invasion, and infiltrative/irregular tumour margins {29537683}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65878,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65879,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65880,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p>Criteria are not well defined for the diagnosis of STUMP in the lower genital tract. However, contemporary studies have validated and recommended the use of conventional uterine methodology and criteria for classification of lower genital tract smooth muscle tumours. See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/241/10909\" target=\"_blank\">#10909</a>Table&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/241/10909\" target=\"_blank\">#10909</a> in the section on STUMP of the uterine corpus.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:04:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65881,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65882,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 501,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prognostic data on lower genital tract STUMPs are limited. However, the few recent studies that classified lower genital smooth muscle tumours as STUMP by uterine smooth muscle tumour criteria found a low risk of malignant potential {28786880; 28180147}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:27:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]